- content_for :title, "Booking links to check"

.admin-page__header
  %h1 Booking links to check

%p.admin-hint
  Automatic links find a property by name and position, and often land on a search of the area instead of its page.
  Until a link is confirmed, the site says it searches for the stay. Open each link: if it lands on this property,
  confirm it; if not, paste the property’s own page on that site. Listed stays only, the most clicked first.
  Opening a link here is not logged as a click.

- if @listings.empty?
  %p Every listed stay’s booking links are confirmed.
- else
  %p= "#{@total} to check#{" (showing the first #{@listings.size})" if @total > @listings.size}."
  .table-wrap
    %table.admin-table
      %thead
        %tr
          %th Property
          %th Site
          %th Clicks
          %th Link
          %th Its own page on the site
          %th
            %span.visually-hidden Confirm
      %tbody
        - @listings.each do |listing|
          - property = listing.property
          %tr
            %td
              = link_to property.name, admin_property_path(property)
              %br
              %small= property.destination.name
            %td= listing.provider_name
            %td= listing.clicks_count
            %td= link_to "Open link", Affiliate::LinkBuilder.new(listing).url, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "button button--small"
            %td
              = form_with model: listing, url: admin_property_listing_path(property, listing), method: :patch do |f|
                = hidden_field_tag :return_to, admin_booking_links_path
                = f.label :url, "#{listing.provider_name} page for #{property.name}", class: "visually-hidden"
                = f.url_field :url, value: "", placeholder: "https://…", required: true
                = f.submit "Save", class: "button button--small"
            %td= button_to "It opens this property", confirm_admin_property_listing_path(property, listing), method: :patch, class: "button button--small"
